Comment (internal/service/relational/evidence/batch.go:279):
**[Should-fix] The "fail pending items" update is written three times**

`Submit` (enqueue failure, line 178), `failChunkOnFinalAttempt` (line 266) and `failItem` (line 279) each build the same `Updates(map[string]any{"status": failed, "error": message, "payload": nil})` against `status = pending`, differing only in the item range. The three must stay in step (for example clearing the payload, or a future `processed_at`), and a change to one is easy to miss in the others.

**Why:** Three copies of the same state transition must change together.
**Fix:** Have one helper, e.g. `failPendingItems(ctx, batchID, first, end int, message string)`, used by all three (Submit passes the whole range, failItem a range of one).
**Severity basis:** no rule matched; decision tree: likely to cause a future bug.

